// ----- 2xx SUCCESS -----

// 200 OK
// Standard success response. Used for successful GET, PUT, PATCH.

// 201 Created
// A new resource was successfully created (typically after POST).

// 204 No Content
// Success, but nothing to send back. Common for DELETE.


// ----- 4xx CLIENT ERRORS -----

// 400 Bad Request
// Malformed request or failed validation (missing field, wrong format, etc).

// 401 Unauthorized
// Client is not authenticated (not logged in / missing or invalid token).

// 403 Forbidden
// Client IS authenticated but doesn't have permission for this action.

// 404 Not Found
// The resource (e.g. an id) doesn't exist.

// 409 Conflict
// Conflicts with current state (duplicate entry, unique constraint, etc).

// 422 Unprocessable Entity
// Well-formed request, but fails business-rule validation.


// ----- 5xx SERVER ERRORS -----

// 500 Internal Server Error
// Generic "something broke" error. Spring's default fallback for
// unhandled exceptions.

// 503 Service Unavailable
// Server temporarily can't handle the request (overloaded, down, etc).


// ----- RULE OF THUMB -----
// 2xx = it worked
// 4xx = you (client) did something wrong
// 5xx = we (server) did something wrong